WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.517
I built ScanSafe because a QR
code hides the one thing I want
to

00:00:04.517 --> 00:00:06.701
check first: where the link goes.

00:00:06.941 --> 00:00:08.755
Let me show you how I use it.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.195
I open ScanSafe, tap Scan QR
Code, and point my camera at the

00:00:14.195 --> 00:00:14.565
code.

00:00:14.805 --> 00:00:18.091
Here’s a photo I took while
testing it on my laptop.

00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:22.280
Once the code is in view, ScanSafe
reads the address and shows me

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.131
what it found.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.621
I can also paste a link
and select Scan.

00:00:26.861 --> 00:00:29.571
In this test, the Google
address scored zero.

00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:33.495
Look at the other address. What
looks like the last letter in

00:00:33.495 --> 00:00:35.549
PayPal is actually the number one.

00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:39.693
ScanSafe flagged that, along with
the word ‘login’ in the link.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.635
When I get a warning, I read the
reasons before deciding what to

00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:44.824
do.

00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:47.240
A low score can still miss something.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.721
To try it yourself, choose ‘Try
ScanSafe’ on this page and run one

00:00:51.721 --> 00:00:52.749
of the examples.
